Third-party data

The ecbackoff code is licensed under MIT above. The bundled reference and
example sequences are subsets of UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot from the UniProt
Consortium (https://www.uniprot.org/uniprot). The reference sequences were
selected from release 2026_04. The reference table combines selected
UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot annotations with data from the ENZYME nomenclature
database, maintained by the Swiss-Prot group at the SIB Swiss Institute
of Bioinformatics (https://enzyme.expasy.org/). The sequences and
annotations were selected and reformatted for ecbackoff.

UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot and the ENZYME database are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

LicenseRef-IUBMB-ExplorEnz

The orphan table (data/orphan.tsv.gz) includes selected EC identifiers,
creation years and accepted names from ExplorEnz, the International Union
of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (IUBMB) Enzyme Nomenclature database
(https://enzyme-database.org/). ExplorEnz entries are copyright 2001-2026
IUBMB. The database authors permit use in other applications with
acknowledgement of the source. See the Availability section of McDonald,
Boyce and Tipton, Nucleic Acids Research 37, D593-D597 (2009),
https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkn582. ecbackoff selects, reformats and ranks
a subset of these records.

Reaction similarity values in the orphan table are calculated from the
Rhea reaction knowledgebase (https://www.rhea-db.org/), available under
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
See https://www.rhea-db.org/help/license-disclaimer.
